# Renter communications privacy

Automatic emails and texts to renters require **per-renter consent** (`people.auto_communications_enabled`, default off).

## Rules for agents

- Never enable automatic communications without staff recording consent on the person record.
- Never add silent, scheduled, or bulk tenant email/SMS paths that bypass consent.
- One-off tenant messages are allowed only via **explicit staff actions** (dedicated button or a default-off `notify` checkbox the office manager opts into).
- Creating invoices must not imply email. Catch-up and period create default to `notify: false`.
- `RENT_COMMUNICATIONS_ENABLED` / `PREVIEW` gate the **daily auto scheduler** (plus preview routing). They do not replace per-renter consent. One-off sends use ACS directly; preview still redirects to `CONTACT_NOTIFY_EMAIL`.
- Staff/ops digests and alert SMS (office pager) are not renter communications and are out of scope for this rule.
- Do not invent tenant SMS until product work adds it; consent wording may already cover future texts under the same flag.
